{"id":"agm-86-alcm","slug":"agm-86-alcm","name":"AGM-86","aliases":["Agm86","CALCM","AGM 86","AGM-86B","AGM-86C/D","AGM-86 CALCM","AGM-86D CALCM","Senior Surprise","AGM-86A Cruise Missile","AGM-86B Cruise Missile","AGM-86 Air-Launched Cruise Missile","AGM-86 Air Launched Cruise Missile","AGM-86 ALCM"],"kind":"missile","category":"cruise-missiles","subcategory":"Air-to-ground strategic cruise missile","description":"The AGM-86 ALCM is an American subsonic air-launched cruise missile (ALCM) built by Boeing and operated by the United States Air Force. This missile was developed to increase the effectiveness and survivability of the Boeing B-52G and B-52H Stratofortress strategic bombers, allowing the aircraft to deliver its payload from a great distance. The missile hampers an enemy force's ability to respond and conduct air defense.","development":"All variants of the AGM-86 missile are powered by a Williams F107 turbofan jet engine that propels it at sustained subsonic speeds and can be launched from aircraft at both high and low altitudes. The missile deploys its folded wings, tail surfaces and engine inlet after launch.\nAGM-86B/C/D missiles increase flexibility in target selection. AGM-86B missiles can be air-launched in large numbers by the bomber force. B-52H bombers carry six AGM-86B or AGM-86C missiles on each of two externally mounted pylons and eight internally on a rotary launcher, giving the B-52H a maximum capacity of 20 missiles per aircraft.\nAn enemy force would have to counterattack each of the missiles individually, making defense against them costly and complicated. The enemy's defenses are further hampered by the missiles' small size and low-altitude flight capability, which makes them difficult to detect on radar.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Propulsion & Guidance","items":[{"label":"Engine","value":"Williams International"},{"label":"Engine","value":"F107-WR-101 turbofan engine"},{"label":"Guidance (AGM-86B)","value":"Litton inertial navigation system element with TERCOM updates"},{"label":"Guidance (AGM 86C)","value":"Litton INS element integrated with multi-channel onboard GPS"},{"label":"Guidance","value":"<!--"},{"label":"Launch Platform","value":"Boeing B-52H Stratofortress"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"1,458 kg (AGM-86B)","numeric":1458,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"1,750 kg (AGM-86C Block 0 and AGM-86D)","numeric":1750,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"1,950 kg (AGM-86C Block 1)","numeric":1950,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"20 ft. 9 in. (6.3 m)","numeric":20,"unit":"ft"},{"label":"Diameter","value":"24.5 in","numeric":24.5,"unit":"in"},{"label":"Wingspan","value":"12 ft","numeric":12,"unit":"ft"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Operational Range (AGM-86B)","value":"1,500+ mi (2,400+ km)"},{"label":"Operational Range (AGM-86C)","value":"classified (nominal 680 miles, 1,100 km)"},{"label":"Speed (AGM-86B)","value":"550 mph (890 km/h, Mach 0.73)","numeric":550,"unit":"mph"},{"label":"Speed (AGM 86C)","value":"classified (nominal high subsonic)"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designed","value":"1974"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Boeing Integrated Defense Systems"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1980"},{"label":"Number Built","value":"1,715 (AGM-86B)"},{"label":"Number Built","value":"239 (AGM-86C)"},{"label":"Number Built","value":"50 (AGM-86D)"},{"label":"Unit Cost","value":"$1 million (AGM-86B)"},{"label":"Unit Cost","value":"additional $160,000 conversion cost for AGM-86C;"},{"label":"Unit Cost","value":"additional $896,000 conversion cost for AGM-86D"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"United States"},{"label":"In Service (AGM-86B)","value":"1982–present"},{"label":"In Service (AGM-86C/D)","value":"retired"}]}],"specIndex":{"Engine":"Williams International","Guidance":"Litton inertial navigation system element with TERCOM updates","Launch Platform":"Boeing B-52H Stratofortress","Wei